+
+# K1X Board Storage Policy
+
+## When to use
+
+Use this before a task writes binaries, models, inputs, outputs, logs, profiles, perf data, temporary files, or caches on a Banana-Pi BPI-F3/K1X board.
+
+## Preflight
+
+Before the first board write, record:
+
+```bash
+hostname
+findmnt -T /data
+df -hT /data /
+lsblk -o NAME,TYPE,FSTYPE,SIZE,MOUNTPOINTS
+test -d /data
+test -w /data
+```
+
+Require `/data` to be writable, backed by a non-`mmcblk` filesystem, and to have enough free space for the stage. If this fails, stop board writes. Do not silently fall back to eMMC.
+
+## Stage Root
+
+Use one stage-owned root:
+
+```bash
+BOARD_STAGE_ROOT="/data/k1x-stage-runs/$STAGE_ID"
+mkdir -p "$BOARD_STAGE_ROOT"/{bin,models,inputs,outputs,logs,profiles,perf,objdump,tmp,cache}
+export TMPDIR="$BOARD_STAGE_ROOT/tmp"
+export XDG_CACHE_HOME="$BOARD_STAGE_ROOT/cache"
+```
+
+Deploy new runners and stage data only below this root. Reuse installed shared libraries in place when appropriate instead of duplicating them.
+
+## eMMC Exceptions
+
+Do not put bulky or persistent stage artifacts under `/home`, `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, or `/root`. A small technically unavoidable exception must record path, bytes, reason, why `/data` could not be used, and cleanup/disposition.
+
+## Cleanup Safety
+
+Never clean broad board directories. Remove only the exact stage-owned root, only after its artifacts are hashed and copied, and only when the task or operator explicitly requests cleanup.
+
+## Required Evidence
+
+Report the storage preflight, stage-root manifest, and eMMC exceptions. Keep board and host artifact hashes with the task's normal raw-evidence log.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `scripts/selftest.sh` after editing this skill.
